proof='''# Independent reconstruction of the fixed-source reset claim

This is an independent review of A003-VACUUM-CALIBRATION-ABSORPTION@1, hash eae891504525bc258746900115643f249fcde92d20afde807551c07569a861d4. A093 supplies no repair. Verdict: the stated finite-law identity, physical pathwise corollary and abstract supplied-likelihood cost consequence hold under their explicit hypotheses. Negative-cell rate18 assembly and upstream source construction are NOT accepted by this review.

1. Quotient representation. Identify two nonconstant references when their nonempty vectors lie on the same positive ray. A calibration chooses the unique representative on this ray with specified empty mass. A positive mass-preserving map fixing the empty atom acts on this quotient: if U=bS+(1-b)delta, then MU=bMS+(1-b)delta. This is a linear identity even when b>1; U and MU themselves remain nonnegative. It follows directly that calibrating either image gives the same normalized law. Thus no convex-mixture assumption is needed. At p=1 the ray disappears; the generic identity for r<1 is false/inadmissible. Physical finite-CE constant parents have only constant descendants, so r=1 closes precisely the claimed endpoint. A source with empty mass1 is likewise physically constant-only.

2. Support. A nonzero Fourier coefficient after restriction is a sum/difference of coefficients in its deleted-coordinate fiber; finite parent CE ensures positive reference mass on at least one such coefficient. Its marginal fiber is therefore positive. Induction proves all nonconstant path calibrations are admissible. Adaptivity does not alter this pointwise argument. The first reset may change the old reference; after it, every same-original-source reset equals current-reference calibration. All unchanged sibling references, including nonzero costs at constant actual leaves, stay present.

3. Independent payment reconstruction. Let D=m delta+N have total<=1 and empty mass m equal to the root actual empty probability. Let normalized S>=D and Q>=m delta+gamma N. For any query fiber of actual mass a, let t be actual query-coordinate occupancy and q the D conditional occupancy. Direct expansion gives parent CE minus mean child CE = a[h(t)+KL(t||q)], summed over fibers. This holds for subprobabilities because each occupied fiber is normalized separately. It pays the erasure and a nonnegative refund. At a retained leaf, D_l=m delta+N_l and Q_l>=m delta+gamma N_l. For u=N_l(empty), weighted AM-GM gives

  (m+gamma u)/(m+u) >= gamma^[u/(m+u)],
  u/(m+u)<=1-m because u<=1-m.

Hence retained excess is at most L[1-m p_l], L=log2(1/gamma), p_l=actual empty probability. Endpoint m=0 or1 follows directly without dividing zero. Reset leaves have no excess: S_l>=D_l decreases CE, and calibrating S_l decreases it further by binary KL. Telescope the full stopped tree. The squared conditional-mean submartingale gives E_leaf p_l>=m. Including only retained leaves reduces the nonnegative penalties, so total excess<=L(1-m^2). Below the first-reset antichain, every later reset is a current-reference calibration by step1 and costs minus a binary KL. No terminal is discarded and no second quota is created. This proves exactly the abstract consequence in A003@1 independently of the A096 helper.

4. Transport boundary. For any actual law P with empty probability p and finite full laws V,S, split cross entropy into the Bernoulli vacuum term and (1-p) times conditional-nonempty CE. Subtracting the costs gives

 CE(P,C_p(S))-CE(P,V)
   =(1-p) E_{P^+} log2(V^+/S^+) - KL_Bern(p||V(empty)).

This independently recovers A003 MINIMAL_TARGET(1). The bank update follows by adding the physical query refund and retaining every old frontier cost. Its affordability inequality is necessary and sufficient for the fixed selected transaction; it supplies no affordable selection or source.

5. Failure control for an overbroad literature inference. On two bits let f be parity, P concentrated on {1,2}, I=2. Its complete two-query tree has signed Cov=-1 and expected occupancy A=2, satisfying prior-stage A=2I+Cov-Var. Let Q uniform on all four labels. For any integer k>=2 choose a full reference S_k with vacuum1/4, each singleton 3(1-2^-k)/8 and pair 3*2^-k/4. Calibration to the true vacuum0 makes pair mass2^-k. Thus CE(P,C_0(S_k))=k, whereas CE(P,C_0(Q))=log2(3) and raw CE(P,Q)=2. Every normalizer and ghost label is included. The physical tree is unchanged as k grows. Therefore the physical covariance/code account alone cannot price arbitrary changed-reference terminal costs. This is a scope control for an already known arbitrary-reset obstruction (compare A090's full-support controls), not a new FEI counterexample: H(f)=0 for this family. It does not refute an influence-priced chosen-source construction or the supplied-floor theorem.

6. Priority and review scope. The reviewed identity is elementary finite linear algebra; its cost proof is the complete-reference chain, binary KL and conditional-mean martingale. No first-result, novel theorem, latest-best bound, published priority or all-Boolean FEI claim follows. The WWW14 source theorem audited last stage pays a complete computing-tree spectral code; it contains no arbitrary changed-reference terminal law. The current audit introduces no new external version/correction claim and reuses the prior pinned primary source. A003's abstract return distinction can be removed; A096's literal repeated-original-source exclusion is superseded only for physical marginalization and pure vacuum calibration. Changes of nonempty shape remain outside that closure.

First unsupported universal line: choose an admitted influence-priced original source AND a useful nonempty-shape-changing transport satisfying the actual signed affordability inequality from the SAME unused bank. A covariance estimate or repeated pure-calibration example does not supply this selection.
'''
write(R/'DERIVATION.md',proof)
statement='Independent review accepts A003-VACUUM-CALIBRATION-ABSORPTION@1 at its exact fixed-source finite-law and supplied-likelihood abstract scope: repeated original-source returns through physical marginals and vacuum calibrations have zero additional charge. It does not accept the upstream negative-cell rate18 assembly or construct an all-Boolean influence-priced source. A fixed actual parity2 physical tree with I=2 and Cov=-1 admits full shape-changing references whose calibrated CE is k for every integer k>=2, so that physical account alone cannot pay arbitrary replacement references.'
